      "body": "Sure! Here\u2019s how you can do it in JupyterLab:\n\n1. **Create a new code cell** (you can do this by clicking the \u201c+ Code\u201d button or pressing `B` to create a new cell below your current one).\n2. In that cell, type the following Python code:\n\n```python\nprint(\"Hello World\")\n```\n\n3. **Run the cell** by pressing **Shift + Enter** (or click the \u201cRun\u201d \u25b6\ufe0f button in the toolbar).\n\nYou should see this output below the cell:\n\n```\nHello World\n```\n\nWould you like me to explain what `print()` does in Python?",
