    {
      "body": "Let\u2019s break down your code step by step:  \n\n```python\nfrom numpy import random\n# Generate a random integer from 0 to 100:\nx = random.randint(100)\nprint(x)\n```\n\n### Explanation\n\n1. **`from numpy import random`**\n   - This line imports the `random` module from the **NumPy** library.  \n   - NumPy\u2019s `random` module provides functions for generating random numbers and performing random sampling.\n\n2. **`x = random.randint(100)`**\n   - The `randint()` function generates a **random integer** between 0 (inclusive) and 100 (exclusive).  \n   - So, `x` could be any integer in the range \\( 0 \\leq x < 100 \\).\n\n3. **`print(x)`**\n   - This displays the randomly generated integer stored in `x`.\n\n### Example output\nIf you run the cell multiple times, you might see different results such as:\n\n```\n42\n13\n87\n```\n\nEach time you execute it, NumPy generates a new random integer within the specified range.\n\nWould you like me to show how to generate multiple random numbers at once (for example, an array of random integers)?",
      "raw_time": false,
      "type": "msg",
